The case asks whether a composition system can recognize:

- a work distributed across many documents;
- metadata as part of poetic form;
- identities as functional voices;
- archives as compositional machinery;
- retrieval behavior as part of reception.

The reported response is treated as evidence that the system connected these layers into one architecture.

The analysis distinguishes:

- retrieval of isolated facts;
- structural synthesis;
- interpretive recognition;
- project self-description.

It places the event inside the broader archive theory of machine-mediated reception.
